     "Seen on thin axial or sagittal T2 (CISS) as a thread leaving the pontomedullary junction and running up the clivus; Dorello's canal and the cavernous segment are seen on contrast T1. Imaging is often normal in microvascular palsies; look for raised pressure signs, clival and petrous apex lesions and cavernous sinus disease.",
